      ]}
    />
  </section>

  <div class="verification">
    <strong>Verification:</strong> Maine 10mg per-serving cap and 200mg per-package cap sourced directly from Maine Revised Statutes Title 28-B §703(1)(F) (the primary statutory source), cross-referenced against the Maine OCP packaging guidance document and mainecannabis.org state law summary. The Title 28-B §701(1)(K) nutritional fact panel requirement, Title 22 §2429-A packaging rules, and Title 28-B §703(1)(D) universal symbol requirement are cited from the same primary statutory source. Dosing chart and onset times sourced from Leafly's edible dosing guide (the cannabis industry's primary-source dosing reference). Beginner dose and overconsumption guidance from Leafly and Quick Med Cards' edible dosage calculator. Special-considerations sections reference CDC and Maine OCP public health guidance. Always start with the lowest dose for your experience level and wait at least 90 minutes before re-dosing.
  </div>

  <p class="disclaimer"><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Information is provided for general reference only and does not constitute medical advice. Cannabis affects individuals differently. Consult a qualified healthcare professional before using cannabis, particularly if you are pregnant, breastfeeding, taking medications, or have a pre-existing health condition. Maine cannabis products sold at licensed dispensaries comply with Maine OCP regulations. Verify any specific product's dose and content directly with the dispensary or by reading the product's Certificate of Analysis (COA).</p>

